  "codex_last_message": "Changed the workspace in two places: `src/db.rs` now has a default-off block-bound pruning experiment for the ANN flat path, and the local harness wrappers under `.meta_codex/tools/` now support `--enable-block-bound-prune` / `--block-bound-dims` in both one-off and sweep flows. I also recorded the cycle in `.meta_codex/strategy.md`, `.meta_codex/research_notes.md`, `.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md`, and `.meta_codex/recent_cycles/cycle_047.json`.\n\nResults were negative for the new ANN branch, so I did not spend the exact ANN gate on it. On the primed `300`-query local gate at `14 / 138 / 384` with `u8` routing, the current flat path measured `6073.53 QPS`, `0.9480` recall; disabling vector-radius pruning dropped to `5775.61`, same recall; block-bound pruning with `8` dims fell further to `4836.42`, same recall, and pruned only about `0.25` vectors/query. I also rechecked true global local-subcluster probing and it stayed far below recall (`~0.59-0.75`), so that path is still parked.\n\nThe kept official state is still valid: `build_project` succeeded, `run_correctness_test` passed at `1.0000` recall, and a fresh serial quick `run_benchmark` reached `11025.40 QPS`, `1.0000` recall. Current score expectation is unchanged: the official default scorer is still roughly low-`11k` quick / low-`12k` full territory on this host, and the best exact ANN expectation remains the existing mid-`5k` flat `u8` branch rather than anything from this cycle.\n\nNext best move: stop spending cycles on selector-only pruning ideas that leave scanned vectors near `12k/query`. The strongest follow-on is a materially stronger shortlist signal, most likely a residual-aware cluster-local PQ/codebook path or a geometry revisit that can actually change the scan budget before rerank.",
